        {
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is the procedure for LLP contribution change in India?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The procedure requires three steps under Section 23(2) of the LLP Act, 2008 read with Rule 21(1) of LLP Rules, 2009: (1) Pass a partners' resolution approving the revised contribution amounts, (2) Execute a Supplementary LLP Agreement on appropriate stamp paper signed by all partners, and (3) File Form LLP-3 on the MCA V3 portal within 30 days of the resolution."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What form is required to file LLP contribution change with MCA?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Form LLP-3 (Part B) is the form required. This is a webform on the MCA V3 portal under LLP e-Filing. Select 'Change in partner's contribution and % of profit sharing' as the reason. Form LLP-4 is NOT required if the change is only in contribution amounts without partner addition or removal."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is the time limit for filing Form LLP-3 after contribution change?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Form LLP-3 must be filed within 30 days of passing the partners' resolution under Rule 21(1) of LLP Rules, 2009. Missing this deadline attracts INR 100 per day of delay as late fee with no cap. Non-filing also blocks Form LLP-8 and Form LLP-11 on the MCA portal."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Is stamp duty applicable on LLP contribution change?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Stamp duty applies to the Supplementary LLP Agreement on contribution increase. The rate depends on the amount of increase and the State Stamp Act applicable to the LLP's registered office state. For contribution decrease, no additional stamp duty is required."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Does changing LLP contribution affect profit sharing ratio?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. A change in capital contribution does not automatically change the profit-sharing ratio unless the LLP Agreement explicitly provides for such a link. Partners may keep the ratio unchanged even after contribution revision. Any intended change must be separately documented."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "What is the penalty for late filing of Form LLP-3?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The late filing penalty is INR 100 per day of delay from the 30-day due date under the LLP Act, 2008 as amended. There is no maximum cap specified on cumulative late fees, making timely filing critical."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "Can LLP contribution be in non-cash form?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. Under Section 32 of the LLP Act, 2008, contribution can include tangible property, intangible property (patents, goodwill), promissory notes, agreements for services, or any other benefit. All non-cash contributions must be valued by a registered valuer per Rule 23(2) of LLP Rules, 2009."
              }
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "name": "LLP contribution change karne ki process kya hai?",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "LLP contribution change ke liye partners ka resolution pass karna hota hai, phir stamped supplementary LLP agreement execute karna hota hai, aur MCA V3 portal par Form LLP-3 Part B file karna hota hai resolution date se 30 din ke andar. Patron Accounting ka CA aur CS team poora process handle karta hai starting at INR 2,499. Quick Answers What form for LLP contribution change? Form LLP-3 (Part B) on MCA V3 portal. Filed within 30 days per Rule 21(1), LLP Rules 2009. Who certifies Form LLP-3? Practising Chartered Accountant, Company Secretary, or Cost Accountant registered on MCA V3. Is Form LLP-4 required? No. Form LLP-4 is for partner addition/removal. Contribution-only change uses Form LLP-3 Part B. Does contribution change affect profit sharing? Not automatically. Only if the LLP Agreement explicitly links contribution to profit ratio."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
